<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bessarabia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bessarabia is a historical region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prut">Prut</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dniester">Dniester</a> rivers in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, the eastern half of the medieval Principality of Moldavia. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> annexed it from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> in 1812. It united with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> in 1918, was taken by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1940, and today forms most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moldova">Republic of Moldova</a>, with its northern and southern fringes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bessarabia.jpg" alt="Bessarabia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ЯдвигаВереск · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81_%D0%90%D0%BA%D0%BA%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B0%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%BE%D1%97_%D1%84%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%82%D0%B5%D1%86%D1%96,_%D0%91%D1%96%D0%BB%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4-%D0%94%D0%BD%D1%96%D1%81%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
